{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:isometry-invariance-riemannian-distance","title":"prop:isometry-invariance-riemannian-distance","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":2294,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#prop:isometry-invariance-riemannian-distance","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:isometry]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-distance]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:metric-preserving-distance-le]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:isometry-symm]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"prop:isometry-invariance-riemannian-distance","line":3704,"source":"\\begin{proposition}[Isometry Invariance of the Riemannian Distance Function]\n\\label{prop:isometry-invariance-riemannian-distance}\n\n\\uses{def:isometry, def:riemannian-distance, lem:metric-preserving-distance-le, lem:isometry-symm}\n\n\n\n\n\\dcref{ch2:2.51}\nIf $\\varphi:(M,g)\\to(\\widetilde M,\\widetilde g)$ is an isometry between connected Riemannian manifolds with or without boundary, then\n\\[\nd_{\\widetilde g}(\\varphi(x),\\varphi(y))=d_g(x,y),\n\\qquad x,y\\in M.\n\\]\n\\end{proposition}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{lem:metric-preserving-distance-le,lem:isometry-symm}\n\\sketch Lemma \\ref{lem:metric-preserving-distance-le} gives one inequality for $\\varphi$. Lemma \\ref{lem:isometry-symm} makes $\\varphi^{-1}$ an isometry, and the same inequality for $\\varphi^{-1}$ gives the reverse bound.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proposition</div></section>[Isometry Invariance of the Riemannian Distance Function] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-70726f703a69736f6d657472792d696e76617269616e63652d7269656d616e6e69616e2d64697374616e6365\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Aisometry\">↗ def:isometry</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ariemannian-distance\">↗ def:riemannian-distance</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ametric-preserving-distance-le\">↗ lem:metric-preserving-distance-le</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Aisometry-symm\">↗ lem:isometry-symm</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch2:2.51</span></span>If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\varphi :(M,g)\\to (\\widetilde M,\\widetilde g)$\">$\\varphi :(M,g)\\to (\\widetilde M,\\widetilde g)$</span> is an isometry between connected Riemannian manifolds with or without boundary, then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  d_{\\widetilde g}(\\varphi (x),\\varphi (y))=d_g(x,y), \\qquad x,y\\in M.  \\]\">\\[  d_{\\widetilde g}(\\varphi (x),\\varphi (y))=d_g(x,y), \\qquad x,y\\in M.  \\]</span>  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ametric-preserving-distance-le\">↗ lem:metric-preserving-distance-le</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Aisometry-symm\">↗ lem:isometry-symm</a> \\sketch Lemma <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ametric-preserving-distance-le\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:metric-preserving-distance-le\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a6d65747269632d70726573657276696e672d64697374616e63652d6c65\">15</a> gives one inequality for <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\varphi $\">$\\varphi $</span>. Lemma <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Aisometry-symm\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:isometry-symm\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a69736f6d657472792d73796d6d\">3</a> makes <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\varphi ^{-1}$\">$\\varphi ^{-1}$</span> an isometry, and the same inequality for <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\varphi ^{-1}$\">$\\varphi ^{-1}$</span> gives the reverse bound. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:metric-preserving-distance-le","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:euclidean-linear-isometry-distance","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:isometry","title":"def:isometry","label":"def:isometry"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-distance","title":"def:riemannian-distance","label":"def:riemannian-distance"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:metric-preserving-distance-le","title":"lem:metric-preserving-distance-le","label":"lem:metric-preserving-distance-le"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:isometry-symm","title":"lem:isometry-symm","label":"lem:isometry-symm"}],"backl